attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a single spine column.** Column 0, `ycjF`, is carried by 100% of chromosomes, persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0% of calls {S1}. The model names 99% of them, at 0.03 bits {S1, M}.

@variable **The rest of the window is fork and variable columns**, 1 to 79, carried by 49 to 87%, 54 persistent and 25 shell {S2}. A branch of 24 families runs through columns 1 to 24, a parallel path carried instead of the most carried families there, 18 persistent and 6 shell, at 10 to 13% {S2.b1}. The `psp` genes, columns 14 to 19, are [[phage shock envelope response]] {S2.c14-19, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine column than on the fork and variable ones**, 99 against 93%, and hesitates less there, 0.03 against 0.37 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 78, `yciI`, is a fork column, at 0.95 bits {H, M}.

@end **The window ends on fork columns.** Columns 75 to 79, `yciB` to `kch`, are carried by 69 to 49% of chromosomes, all persistent {S2.c75-79}. The last column is `kch`, in 49% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 93% of genes**, 0.37 bits on average, perplexity 1.4 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.77 against 0.21 bits, and names fewer genes, 85% against 96% {C}.

